&Q000577 = Letter from a governor and temple administrator to a king
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.3.05
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.3.05&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div version 1 (Version A (from Nibru))

1.1. lugal-me u₃-na-dug₄
#lem: lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: Say to our king what the  
#etcsl: line-id=1.1

1.2. ensi₂ saŋŋa-ke₄ na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: ensik[ruler]; saŋŋa[an official]; e[speak]
#tr.en: governor and temple administrator say: 
#etcsl: line-id=1.2

1.3. [a]-šag₄# da-ab-ta{ki} šar₂-šar₂-šar₂{iku}-bi
#lem: ašag[field]; Dabta[1]ON; šar[3600]
#tr.en: The three @fsux{šar} (i.e. 3,240 @fsux{iku}) of the  
#etcsl: line-id=1.3

1.4. eš₂-gar₃ {d}en-lil₂ (1::1) u₃ {d}nin-urta
#lem: ešgar[work assignment]; Enlil[1]DN; u[and]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: field @wON{Dabta} are assigned for the benefit of @wDN{Enlil} @vart[t3305.1.v1,t3305.1.v1]{@varn{2 mss. add:} @wDN{, Ninlil} } and @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.4

:4v.1.1: ($2 mss. add:$) {d}nin-lil₂
#lem: Ninlil[1]DN

1.5. šag₄-bi-ta (1:bur₃-bur₃-bur₃{iku}-am₃:1) šukur₂ lu₂ niŋ₂-dab₅-ba-ke₄-ne
#lem: šag[heart]; bur[unit of area]; šukur[food allocation]; lu[person]; niŋdab[requisitions]
#tr.en: Of this, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.5

:5v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) |U×KASKAL|-|U×KASKAL|-|U×KASKAL|{iku}-am₃
#lem: U@g[unit of area]

## :5v.1.1: (1 ms. has instead:$) BUR3@g-BUR3@g-BUR3@g{iku}-am3

1.6. bur₃{iku}-am₃ sa-dur₂ a-šag₄-ga-bi
#lem: bur[unit of area]; sadur[bottom]; ašag[field]
#tr.en: @varh[t3305.1.v2]{three @fsux{bur} (i.e. 54 @fsux{iku}) } @vart[t3305.1.v3,t3305.1.v2]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} three @fsux{BURgunû} (i.e. 540 @fsux{iku}) } are the portion of the men in charge of the requisitions. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.6

1.7. {m}iq-bi-sum₂ u₃ a-bi-qa₂-ti-e inim mu-da-an-ŋar-re-eš
#lem: Iqbisum[1]PN; u[and]; Abiqati[1]PN; inim[word]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: @wPN{Iqbisum} and @wPN{Abī-qātī} have made a claim over one @fsux{bur} (i.e. 18 @fsux{iku}) at the bottom of the field. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.7

1.8. tukum-bi lugal-me an-na-kam
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]; anna[approval]
#tr.en: If our king consents, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.8

1.9. ra-gaba hu-mu-ši-in-gi₄-gi₄-ma
#lem: ragaba[rider]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: he should send a courier and should ……  
#etcsl: line-id=1.9

1.10. kiŋ₂ a-ak bulug a#-šag₄ inim dug₄ hu-mu-ni-ib-[...]
#lem: kiŋ[work]; ak[do]; bulug[needle]; ašag[field]; inim[word]; dug[speak]; X
#tr.en: the instructions for doing the work and for the boundary stakes of the field. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.10

1.11. SU-bi-še₃ 2(aš) iku X bur₃# eše₃-eše₃{iku#} gaba a-šag₄-ga-bi
#lem: X; n; iku[unit of area]; X; bur[unit of area]; eše[unit of area]; gaba[breast]; ašag[field]
#tr.en: Two @fsux{iku} at its …… and the …… area facing the field have been hoed and worked upon. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.11

1.12. {ŋiš}al-ta ba-dub₂ kiŋ₂-še₃ ba-ak
#lem: al[hoe]; dub[tremble]; kiŋ[work]; ak[do]
#tr.en: Workers, extra labourers, farmers, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.12

1.13. erin₂ tah-hu-um engar šag₄-gud lu₂ {ŋiš}apin-na nu-me-a
#lem: erin[people]; tahhum[replacement]; engar[farmer]; šagud[ox driver]; lu[person]; apin[(seed) plow]; me[be]
#tr.en: ox-drivers and ploughmen being unavailable, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.13

1.14. gud dili-dili-ta a-šag₄ ŋiš bi₂-ur₃
#lem: gud[bull]; dili[single]; ašag[field]; ŋeš[tree]; ur[drag]
#tr.en: the field has been harrowed with single oxen and we do the work with hoes. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.14

1.15. al i₃-ak-en-de₃-en lugal-me he₂-en-zu
#lem: al[hoe]; ak[do]; lugal[king]; zu[know]
#tr.en: Our king should know this. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.15

@end version

