2.6. al-ta ba-dub₂ erin₂-ta he₂-X-a
#lem: al[hoe]; dub[tremble]; erin[people]; X
#tr.en: Two @fsux{iku} which are at its  
#etcsl: line-id=2.6

$ (scribal error for erin2 tah-hu-um)
2.7. kiŋ₂-še₃ sar a-šag₄-ga lu₂ apin-bi nu-bi
#lem: kiŋ[work]; sar[unit of area]; ašag[field]; lu[person]; apin[(seed) plow]; nu[not]
#tr.en: …… have been hoed and ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=2.7

2.8. iq-bi-sum₂ u₃ a!-bi-qa₂-ti#
#lem: Iqbisum[1]PN; u[and]; Abiqati[1]PN
#tr.en: Ploughmen are not available for work  
#etcsl: line-id=2.8

2.9. inim mu-e-de-ŋar-re-eš
#lem: inim[word]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: on a plot in the field. 
#etcsl: line-id=2.9

2.10. tukum-bi lugal-ŋu₁₀
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: @wPN{Iqbisum} and @wPN{Abī-qātī} have made a claim against you. 
#etcsl: line-id=2.10

2.11. an-na-kam
#lem: anna[approval]
#tr.en: If my king consents, 
#etcsl: line-id=2.11

2.12. ra-gaba hu-mu-un-gi₄-gi₄
#lem: ragaba[rider]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: he should send a courier. 
#etcsl: line-id=2.12

2.13. kiŋ₂ ak bulug a-šag₄-ga-bi
#lem: kiŋ[work]; ak[do]; bulug[needle]; ašag[field]
#tr.en: They …… the instructions for  
#etcsl: line-id=2.13

2.14. inim dug₄-ga₁₄ mu-ni-ib-X-ne#
#lem: inim[word]; dug[speak]; X
#tr.en: doing the work and for the boundary stakes of the field. 
#etcsl: line-id=2.14

@end version







